.TH "iwatch" "" "" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
iwatch - A file monitor that runs a command when events happen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
iwatch [options] FILES CMD...
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run \f[V]CMD\f[R] every time one of \f[V]FILE(s)\f[R] is written to.
If a previous run of \f[V]CMD\f[R] is still running when an event
happens, it is sent the \f[V]TERM\f[R] signal and waited on before
starting a new run of \f[V]CMD\f[R] (this is useful for server type
programs).
.PP
\f[V]FILE(s)\f[R]: A comma, space, or newline separated list of files
\f[B]or\f[R] a \f[V]FILESPEC\f[R].
The \f[V]FILE(s)\f[R] argument must be a single argument so either use
quotes if separating with spaces or newlines, or use commas.
See FILESPEC below.
.PP
\f[V]CMD...\f[R]: Command to run when an event happens.
Percent signs in \f[V]CMD...\f[R] are resolved to references to one or
all of the watched files.
See section \f[V]PERCENT
RESOLUTION\f[R]
.PP
Note that \f[V]CMD...\f[R] can be multiple arguments.
All arguments after the \f[V]FILE(s)\f[R] argument are used for the
command.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS \f[V]-i EVENTS\f[R]
.PP
Ignore \f[V]EVENTS\f[R] where \f[V]EVENTS\f[R] is a comma separated list
of event names to ignore.
.PP
It can be desirable to ignore certain events.
For example running \f[V]git status\f[R] will cause \f[V]OPEN\f[R]
events on tracked files.
.PP
However, some editors only produce \f[V]OPEN\f[R] events.
In this case, we can run the command with \f[V]-i \[dq]\[dq]\f[R] so
that no event is ignored.
.SS \f[V]-s SECONDS\f[R]
.PP
To avoid reacting to groups of events, the main loop of the program
sleeps for 2 seconds before starting to check for new events.
.SS \f[V]-n\f[R]
.PP
Disable resolution of percent signs in \f[V]CMD...\f[R] as described in
the \f[V]FILESPEC\f[R] section.
.SS \f[V]-h\f[R]
.PP
Print a short help message and exit.
.SH PERCENT RESOLUTION
.PP
Inside \f[V]CMD...\f[R], percent signs may be used to refer to the files
being watched so as to not need to repeat them:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]%\f[R] expands to the first of the watched files
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]%\[ha]\f[R] expands to the complete list of watched files
.PP
for example:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
iwatch myscript.py python3 %
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
to watch a python script and run it, or
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
iwatch myscript.sh ./%
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
for a shell script.
.SH FILESPEC
.PP
If the \f[V]FILE\f[R] argument starts with \f[V]\[at]<path>\f[R], then
\f[V]iwatch\f[R] will watch all files tracked by git \f[V]<path>\f[R]
relative to PWD (even if <path> starts with a \[aq]/\[aq]) and for
\f[V]\[at]:<path>\f[R]
.SH CAVEATS
.PP
\f[V]CMD\f[R] is run whenever certain events happen to the watched files
so not exactly when the file is written to.
Other events are ignored like opening the file which happens very
frequently if we have an LSP running.
.SH BUGS AND CONTRIBUTIONS
.PP
Please submit an issue on <https://github.com/philippecarphin/iwatch> or
submit a merge request with any improvements.
.SH LORE
.PP
The \[aq]i\[aq] in \[aq]iwatch\[aq] is for inodes.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Philippe Carphin
